{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["[And kindness — this is the reward of the righteous, which is forever; and it is mentioned in the Torah for those who love Him, who are of the highest rank, and afterward —] <b>to those who keep His commandments</b>: out of fear. And thus its interpretation here: <b>to those who fear Him</b> and <b>those who keep His covenant</b> — only <b>those who remember His commandments</b>; these are the lovers, for His commandments are always before them and in their heart they are not forgotten for a single moment."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 103, :notes {0 "The opening bracketed text appears to be a parenthetical excursus on 'and kindness' from the preceding verse (103:17), before Ibn Ezra turns to the lemma of 103:18."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:04.037752646Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}